CloudBurrow patch 107 to github.com/goccy/googlesqlite v0.3.1
(cloudburrow/cloudburrow#2134).

The bug: a spec case of the patch tests hung for ten minutes inside the
analyzer on main CI (run 44954090598), in absl's hash-set probe loop,
which also stalled every other goroutine behind the garbage collector's
stop-the-world, and go test's timeout killed the package without naming
the case. The hang was a go-googlesql handle freed by its finalizer
before the call that read it (newSimpleCatalog's LanguageOptions, read by
AddGoogleSQLFunctions2); go-googlesql 0108 and tools/bqengine's
handle-keepalive rewrite fix that in the bindings, for every method.

This patch is the guard: the spec runner gets a per-test timeout (4
minutes, or GOOGLESQLITE_PER_TEST_TIMEOUT), which names the overdue
cases, and, when GOOGLESQLITE_TEST_TRACE names a file, logs each case's
start and end there, so a hang that also freezes the watchdog still names
its case.

